Gives the simulated Mid360 the IMU the real one has inside it.

Generated against unitree_mujoco ae6a8403e272733e9996ef59990880330496177f.
FAST-LIO needs the IMU in the laser's housing: the pelvis IMU sits below three waist joints the
gait swings, which no fixed extrinsic absorbs. The site uses Livox's published lidar-in-IMU
offset. The sensors are appended, so the bridge's nu-sized blocks do not shift. No noise model,
matching the pelvis IMU.

